WEBVTT

1
00:01:06.825 --> 00:01:08.840
<v><b>Izzy:</b></v> You can do this.

2
00:01:12.831 --> 00:01:16.005
<v><b>Pamela:</b></v> Oh, hey, Izzy! Good luck!

3
00:01:16.955 --> 00:01:18.647
<v><b>Izzy:</b></v> Thanks, Pamela.

4
00:01:19.464 --> 00:01:21.422
<v><b>Pamela:</b></v> What time’s the interview?

5
00:01:22.087 --> 00:01:23.588
<v><b>Izzy:</b></v> It’s at four p.m.

6
00:01:24.158 --> 00:01:25.622
<v><b>Pamela:</b></v> Are you nervous?

7
00:01:26.933 --> 00:01:30.525
<v><b>Izzy:</b></v> Well, a little bit.

8
00:01:30.754 --> 00:01:36.968
<v><b>Pamela:</b></v> Don’t worry! It’s going to be fine. They’re going to love you.

9
00:02:09.697 --> 00:02:13.346
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Ben. Ben. Can you hear me? I’m driving.

10
00:02:13.802 --> 00:02:17.147
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> Yes, I can hear you, Jenny. Is everything OK?

11
00:02:17.261 --> 00:02:22.241
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Ben, listen. It’s your sister. She had an accident this morning. I’m going to the hospital now.

12
00:02:22.592 --> 00:02:25.747
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> Emma? An accident? Is she OK?

13
00:02:25.757 --> 00:02:29.720
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> A car accident. You need to come home today. I bought you a plane ticket.

14
00:02:29.729 --> 00:02:32.837
Check your email. You’re on the eight o’clock flight this evening.

15
00:02:32.884 --> 00:02:34.623
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> Is she OK?

16
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:38.662
<v><b>Jenny:</b></v> Ben? I can’t hear you. The signal’s really bad.

17
00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:43.442
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> Jenny, I can’t hear you. Is she OK?

18
00:03:07.522 --> 00:03:17.410
<v><b>Izzy:</b></v> OK. I think this works here, but maybe…What about this?

19
00:03:21.425 --> 00:03:23.744
<v><b>Ola:</b></v> Yes, I like that.

20
00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:34.902
<v><b>Max:</b></v> Did you say something?

21
00:04:35.359 --> 00:04:38.628
<v><b>Izzy:</b></v> No, nothing. I think it was the door.

22
00:04:58.907 --> 00:05:06.471
<v><b>Ben:</b></v> Hey, Izzy. I hope the interview went well. Listen, I got some bad news from home.

23
00:05:06.927 --> 00:05:12.553
My sister, Emma, was in a car accident. I’m going back to the US tonight.

24
00:05:13.066 --> 00:05:20.042
I’m on the eight p.m. flight from Gatwick Airport. I’m on my way to Victoria Station. Call me.

25
00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:33.498
<v><b>Ben’s voicemail:</b></v> This is Ben. I can’t take your call, please leave a message.